  "body": "What happens: PR #2138's re-read `acquit_traverses_by_prior` (crates/sim/src/verify/prior_traverse.rs) acquits a convicted rapid at the clearance plane when what the program ahead left standing is under the tip. Its stated law treats \"outside what the map models\" two ways: a capsule part that falls off the stock grid is clamped away and reads as air (module doc: \"off the grid is outside the stock (air)\"), while a column whose height is not a number reads as unknown, and unknown is never proof of air (module doc, line 23, and the #1056 fidelity law). The doc backs the first reading with a condition: the solid law shares the conviction, and an off-grid part \"must not be acquitted with the column's\".\n\nExpected: prove that condition for every mode that reaches the re-read, or make off-grid read as unknown, like a non-number column. Fails closed is the sim's rule.\n\nEvidence: prior_traverse.rs lines 19-34 (the law and the clamped index box, lines 113-118) and clearance_stock.rs line 81 (None prior: no acquittal). Found while reviewing #2138 (lane comment 6911362655, non-blocking note). The reviewer found no failing case.\n\nDone means: a unit test shows a part that stands off the stock grid, under a rapid at the clearance plane, keeps its conviction through the prior re-read in every mode that uses it; or the off-grid branch reads as unknown, with a comment naming why.\n",
